cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the PACT (ASPLOS 2026) and Tierce (SOSP 2026) papers below."
title: "PACT: A Criticality-First Design for Tiered Memory"
abstract: >-
  PACT is a user-space Linux runtime for tiered memory. It attaches to an
  unmodified process and places pages by the CPU stall time they cause (their
  Per-page Access Criticality, PAC) rather than by access frequency alone,
  combining PEBS sampling, per-tier memory-level-parallelism estimates,
  adaptive binning, and kernel page migration.
type: software
